{"vid":"1AaUK6pT_cE","source":"1AaUK6pT_cE.en-orig.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.4,"txt":"when we look at a DC motor we first see"},{"t":3.4,"txt":"the metal protective casing which forms"},{"t":5.6,"txt":"the stator"},{"t":6.8,"txt":"at one end we have the tip of a shaft"},{"t":9,"txt":"protruding through the casing we can"},{"t":11.3,"txt":"attach gears fan blades or even pulleys"},{"t":13.6,"txt":"onto this on the other end we have a"},{"t":15.8,"txt":"plastic end cap with two terminals we"},{"t":18.5,"txt":"can connect a power supply to these"},{"t":20.3,"txt":"terminals to rotate the shaft"},{"t":22.6,"txt":"if we remove the casing to look inside"},{"t":24.5,"txt":"the motor we first find two magnets"},{"t":27.1,"txt":"inside these are permanent magnets which"},{"t":30,"txt":"form a North and South Pole"},{"t":32.4,"txt":"running through the center of the motor"},{"t":34.3,"txt":"we see this Rod which is called the"},{"t":36.7,"txt":"shaft the shaft is used to transfer"},{"t":39.1,"txt":"mechanical energy attached to the shaft"},{"t":41.6,"txt":"we have the rotor the rotor is made from"},{"t":44.5,"txt":"a number of discs which are laminated"},{"t":46.3,"txt":"together"},{"t":47.3,"txt":"each disc has these t-shaped arms cut"},{"t":49.5,"txt":"into them wrapped around These t-shaped"},{"t":51.9,"txt":"Arms of the rotor are the coil windings"},{"t":54.1,"txt":"which carry the electrical current from"},{"t":56,"txt":"the battery"},{"t":57.1,"txt":"as the current passes through the coils"},{"t":59.3,"txt":"it produces an electromagnetic field we"},{"t":62.4,"txt":"control the timing and the polarity of"},{"t":64.7,"txt":"the magnetic field to create rotation"},{"t":67.3,"txt":"the ends of the coils are connected to"},{"t":69.4,"txt":"the commutator"},{"t":70.7,"txt":"the commutator is a ring which has been"},{"t":73,"txt":"segmented into a number of plates which"},{"t":75.1,"txt":"sit concentrically around the shaft"},{"t":77.9,"txt":"these plates are separated and"},{"t":79.6,"txt":"electrically isolated from each other as"},{"t":81.8,"txt":"well as the shaft"},{"t":83.1,"txt":"the ends of each coil connect to a"},{"t":85,"txt":"different commutator plate they do this"},{"t":87.2,"txt":"to create a circuit and we'll see that"},{"t":89.2,"txt":"in detail just shortly"},{"t":90.8,"txt":"sitting within the plastic back cover"},{"t":92.6,"txt":"are the brushes brush arms and terminals"},{"t":96.1,"txt":"the commutator plate sit between the two"},{"t":98.3,"txt":"brushes"},{"t":99.4,"txt":"the brushes rub against the commutator"},{"t":101.4,"txt":"segments to complete the circuit"},{"t":103.6,"txt":"electricity can then flow through a"},{"t":105.8,"txt":"terminal through the arm into the brush"},{"t":108.4,"txt":"through a commutator segment into a coil"},{"t":111.5,"txt":"then out to another commutator segment"},{"t":113.6,"txt":"onto the opposite brush and arm and back"},{"t":116.6,"txt":"to the other terminal"},{"t":118,"txt":"these components give us our basic DC"},{"t":120.5,"txt":"motor"},{"t":121.8,"txt":"the simplest DC motor has just a single"},{"t":124.4,"txt":"coil these are a much simpler design the"},{"t":127.9,"txt":"problem though is that they can align"},{"t":129.6,"txt":"magnetically which jams the motor and"},{"t":131.9,"txt":"stops it from rotating"},{"t":133.5,"txt":"the more sets of coils we have the"},{"t":135.8,"txt":"smoother the rotation will be this is"},{"t":138.1,"txt":"especially useful for low speed"},{"t":139.8,"txt":"applications therefore we normally find"},{"t":142.7,"txt":"at least three coils in a rotor to"},{"t":145,"txt":"ensure smooth rotation"},{"t":147.1,"txt":"each coil is positioned 120 degrees from"},{"t":150.2,"txt":"previous"},{"t":151.4,"txt":"between each coil we find a commutator"},{"t":153.7,"txt":"plate each coil is connected with two"},{"t":156.7,"txt":"commutator plates"},{"t":158.3,"txt":"the plates are electrically isolated"},{"t":160.3,"txt":"from each other except that they are now"},{"t":162.4,"txt":"connected via the coils so if we connect"},{"t":165.2,"txt":"the positive and negative terminals to"},{"t":167.4,"txt":"two of the commutator plates we can"},{"t":169.7,"txt":"complete the circuit current will now"},{"t":171.6,"txt":"flow and a magnetic field will generate"},{"t":173.8,"txt":"in the coils"},{"t":176.8,"txt":"the rotor or Armature is made from"},{"t":179.4,"txt":"multiple discs of iron which are"},{"t":181.2,"txt":"laminated together"},{"t":182.8,"txt":"each disc is electrically insulated from"},{"t":185.2,"txt":"one another with a lack of coating"},{"t":187.3,"txt":"if the Armature was a single piece of"},{"t":189.6,"txt":"solid metal large Eddy currents would"},{"t":191.9,"txt":"swirl around inside these are caused by"},{"t":194.8,"txt":"induced electromotive force or emfs the"},{"t":198.4,"txt":"Eddy currents affect the efficiency of"},{"t":200.3,"txt":"the motor"},{"t":201.3,"txt":"to reduce the Eddy currents Engineers"},{"t":203.5,"txt":"segment the rotor into insulated discs"},{"t":205.9,"txt":"this way the Eddy currents will still"},{"t":208.1,"txt":"flow but they will be much smaller the"},{"t":210.7,"txt":"thinner the disc the smaller the Eddy"},{"t":212.5,"txt":"currents will be"},{"t":215.6,"txt":"the commutator consists of small copper"},{"t":218.2,"txt":"plates which are mounted to the shaft"},{"t":220.4,"txt":"each plate is electrically isolated from"},{"t":222.6,"txt":"one another as well as the shaft"},{"t":224.7,"txt":"the end of each coil is connected to a"},{"t":226.9,"txt":"different commutator plate in this"},{"t":229.1,"txt":"design each commutator plate is"},{"t":231,"txt":"connected with two coils the plates"},{"t":233.5,"txt":"deliver electricity to the coils"},{"t":236.2,"txt":"to get the electricity from the battery"},{"t":238.1,"txt":"and into the plates we have some brushes"},{"t":240.6,"txt":"which rub against the plates the brush"},{"t":243.2,"txt":"arms hold these in place"},{"t":245.5,"txt":"when we complete the circuit electricity"},{"t":247.8,"txt":"will flow into the commutator segment"},{"t":249.8,"txt":"via the brushes and then it will flow"},{"t":252.2,"txt":"into one or two coils as a path becomes"},{"t":254.8,"txt":"available"},{"t":256.1,"txt":"at certain points in the rotation the"},{"t":258.5,"txt":"brushes will come into contact with two"},{"t":260.3,"txt":"plates"},{"t":261.5,"txt":"this will create an arc and we get these"},{"t":263.4,"txt":"small bursts of blue light as this"},{"t":265.3,"txt":"occurs"},{"t":266.8,"txt":"these arcs as well as friction will"},{"t":268.8,"txt":"eventually destroy the brushes over time"},{"t":270.8,"txt":"okay guys that's it for this video but"},{"t":273.5,"txt":"to continue your learning then check out"},{"t":275.1,"txt":"one of the videos on screen now and I'll"},{"t":277,"txt":"catch you there for the next lesson"},{"t":278.8,"txt":"don't forget to follow us on Facebook"},{"t":280.6,"txt":"Twitter Instagram LinkedIn as well as"},{"t":282.7,"txt":"the engineeringmindset.com"}],"words":[{"t":0.359,"w":"when"},{"t":0.96,"w":"we"},{"t":1.14,"w":"look"},{"t":1.26,"w":"at"},{"t":1.5,"w":"a"},{"t":1.62,"w":"DC"},{"t":1.92,"w":"motor"},{"t":2.159,"w":"we"},{"t":2.94,"w":"first"},{"t":3.12,"w":"see"},{"t":3.36,"w":"the"},{"t":3.6,"w":"metal"},{"t":3.78,"w":"protective"},{"t":4.38,"w":"casing"},{"t":4.799,"w":"which"},{"t":5.16,"w":"forms"},{"t":5.58,"w":"the"},{"t":5.759,"w":"stator"},{"t":6.779,"w":"at"},{"t":7.319,"w":"one"},{"t":7.44,"w":"end"},{"t":7.62,"w":"we"},{"t":7.98,"w":"have"},{"t":8.099,"w":"the"},{"t":8.28,"w":"tip"},{"t":8.46,"w":"of"},{"t":8.639,"w":"a"},{"t":8.76,"w":"shaft"},{"t":9,"w":"protruding"},{"t":9.599,"w":"through"},{"t":9.84,"w":"the"},{"t":10.019,"w":"casing"},{"t":10.44,"w":"we"},{"t":11.099,"w":"can"},{"t":11.28,"w":"attach"},{"t":11.519,"w":"gears"},{"t":12.059,"w":"fan"},{"t":12.36,"w":"blades"},{"t":12.719,"w":"or"},{"t":12.9,"w":"even"},{"t":13.019,"w":"pulleys"},{"t":13.